    <location value="194"/>
    <location value="481"/>
    <location value="216"/>
<![CDATA[A common error when working with  NULL  is to assume that it is not possible to insert a zero or an empty string into a column defined as  NOT NULL , but this is not the case. These are in fact values, whereas  NULL means 'not having a value.' You can test this easily enough by using  IS [NOT] NULL  as shown:]]>  </text>
  <code>
    <location value="85"/>
    <location value="221"/>
    <location value="482"/>
    <location value="260"/>
<![CDATA[mysql>  SELECT 0 IS NULL, 0 IS NOT NULL, '' IS NULL, '' IS NOT NULL; +-----------+---------------+------------+----------------+ | 0 IS NULL | 0 IS NOT NULL | '' IS NULL | '' IS NOT NULL | +-----------+---------------+------------+----------------+ |         0 |             1 |          0 |              1 | +-----------+---------------+------------+----------------+]]>  </code>
